WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:05.201
Marvel's What If...? comics have taken readers
into unexplored corners of the Marvel Universe

00:00:05.201 --> 00:00:10.360
for decades, and with a Disney+ animated series
in the works, audiences will soon see some

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:12.860
of these intriguing scenarios explored onscreen.

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:15.340
Here's a look at some of the most highly anticipated
options.

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:21.120
One of the most thought-provoking issues of
the What If...? comic series is "What If Captain

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.960
America Hadn't Vanished During World War Two?"

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:29.539
In that alternate reality, Cap and Bucky continued
their heroic adventures well into the 1960s,

00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:33.700
until Bucky takes up the stars and stripes
so Rogers can become the first director of

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:34.200
SHIELD.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:39.060
The thought of Cap and Bucky returning to
fight crime in a post-WWII America has some

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:44.030
very appealing Batman and Robin-esque vibes,
but the real draw is seeing how those two

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:47.560
might have interacted with the various MCU
characters of that era.

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:52.100
Having Steve Rogers visit Howard and Maria
Stark in the hospital to congratulate them

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:56.120
on the birth of their first son would be just
one of a few intriguing twists.

00:00:57.080 --> 00:01:00.580
"I tell ya, that kid's not even here yet,
and there's nothing I wouldn't do for him."

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:10.740
Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 2 revealed that
Yondu originally abducted Peter Quill from

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:14.420
Earth so he could return him to his father,
Ego the Living Planet.

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:19.240
Fortunately for the young space pirate, Yondu
grew attached to the lad, raising him to become

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:19.740
a Ravager.

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:24.800
Had Yondu made good on his assignment and
returned Quill to Ego, the MCU would've been

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:25.880
majorly affected.

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:30.560
Ego would've been able to harness Quill's
ultra-powerful energy to consume the universe

00:01:30.579 --> 00:01:35.149
with the planetary seeds he'd planted, and
he might even have achieved his goal of galactic

00:01:35.149 --> 00:01:35.700
domination.

00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:39.300
Had Ego's plan gone off without a hitch, who
could've stopped it?

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:43.920
We know Quill was abducted in 1988, so most
of the current members of Earth's Mightiest

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:45.240
Heroes wouldn't be around yet.

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:50.140
Captain America would still be frozen, Tony
Stark wouldn't be Iron Man yet, and Bruce

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:52.060
Banner would still just be a scientist.

00:01:52.580 --> 00:01:57.140
However, at least one potential power could
stand in Ego's way: Captain Marvel.

00:01:57.480 --> 00:02:02.380
Carol Danvers, a member of the intergalactic
Kree force around the time of Quill's abduction,

00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:04.599
would be the most logical first line of defense.

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:09.819
Getting to see the most powerful Avenger battle
a living planet sounds like just the sort

00:02:09.819 --> 00:02:14.349
of thing What If…? should be doing, especially
since it's animated and can thus pull off

00:02:14.349 --> 00:02:15.740
these sorts of big action scenes.

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:21.700
Speaking of Yondu abducting young Earthlings,
what if the blue alien had taken another child

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:22.380
entirely?

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:27.900
Speaking to Discussing Film, What If...? showrunner
Ashley Bradley teased an episode of the series

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:30.180
featuring T'Challa as Star-Lord:

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:34.599
"We wanted to see what if the worlds of Black
Panther and the Guardians of the Galaxy collided

00:02:34.599 --> 00:02:38.849
[...] It's super exciting to work on because,
again, it's seeing these characters and seeing

00:02:38.849 --> 00:02:40.840
the combination of character interactions."

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:46.220
In this reality, was T'Challa taken as a child
instead of Peter Quill, leaving him to eventually

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:50.640
become Star-Lord and assemble the galaxy's
favorite ragtag crew of heroes?

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:55.680
If so, does that leave Shuri to rule Wakanda
as queen as well as Black Panther?

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:57.500
How would Killmonger play into all this?

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:02.680
At the end of Thor: The Dark World, Thor is
given the opportunity to take up his birthright

00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:03.900
and become King of Asgard.

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:09.159
Instead, he chooses to live on Midgard with
Jane Foster, leaving the door open for the

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:11.360
reign of Loki impersonating Odin.

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:16.400
This also leaves Thor free to assist the Avengers
on various missions before heading back home

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:17.560
in Thor: Ragnarok.

00:03:17.969 --> 00:03:22.560
How different would things have been had Thor
decided to rule Asgard and protect the nine

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:23.460
realms instead?

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:28.840
For one, you could argue that an observant
King Thor would've really complicated Thanos'

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:29.360
plans.

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:35.480
In Avengers: Infinity War, Thor, Groot and
Rocket travel to Nidavellir in hopes of forging

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:40.150
a new "Thanos-killing" weapon, only to find
it devastated by the Mad Titan.

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:44.730
Had the real King of Asgard been watching,
this kind of planetary destruction would've

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:47.080
surely sparked Asgard's involvement.

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:51.800
You could even argue that many of the events
of Thor: Ragnarok would've been entirely avoided

00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:56.260
had a dutiful king been in charge, including
the death of Odin and subsequent return of

00:03:56.260 --> 00:03:56.760
Hela.

00:03:57.040 --> 00:04:00.280
Loki's rule, although brief, had far-reaching
implications.

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:05.420
The Battle of New York was the first time
the original six Avengers teamed up, but the

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:08.400
collaboration wasn't exactly a smooth transition.

00:04:08.780 --> 00:04:12.560
What would've happened had one or two of the
heroes simply not been up to the task?

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:17.800
Every member's contribution was crucial to
the victory, and without the full team assembled,

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:20.360
Loki and the Chitauri could've conceivably
won.

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:21.040
What then?

00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:25.400
Since Loki was working for Thanos, the Mad
Titan could've done to Earth exactly what

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:26.600
he did to Gamora's home planet.

00:04:27.340 --> 00:04:31.870
After wiping out half of Earth's population,
he might even have made good on his word and

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:33.220
left Loki in charge of the planet.

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:37.900
It would be interesting to see what a decimated
Earth would look like with Loki as king.

00:04:38.180 --> 00:04:39.920
Which heroes would rise to challenge his rule?

00:04:40.820 --> 00:04:45.620
Whatever happened to Emil Blonsky, a.k.a.
Abomination in The Incredible Hulk?

00:04:45.940 --> 00:04:52.360
Aside from a throwaway mention in an episode
of ABC's Agents of SHIELD, the souped-up Marine-turned-monstrosity

00:04:52.360 --> 00:04:55.380
has seemingly been on ice longer than Captain
America.

00:04:55.660 --> 00:05:00.090
You have to wonder how a character that powerful
has existed in the MCU for so long without

00:05:00.090 --> 00:05:01.340
making a second appearance.

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:06.580
What if, when assembling his vision of the
Avengers, Nick Fury decided to recruit Abomination

00:05:06.590 --> 00:05:09.110
for the team's muscle instead of the Hulk?

00:05:09.110 --> 00:05:12.389
Blonsky sort of makes more sense, due to his
military background.

00:05:12.389 --> 00:05:17.349
Plus, he's apparently been in a special prison
since the events of The Incredible Hulk, whereas

00:05:17.349 --> 00:05:21.419
Banner was a fugitive; it would've been a
lot easier to recruit someone who had a definite

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:21.920
location.

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:26.700
With a lot of training and an attitude adjustment,
Blonsky could've conceivably worked as an

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:27.200
Avenger.

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:31.840
After all, it's not like the team is opposed
to adding members who were initially foes,

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:33.640
like Quicksilver and Scarlet Witch.

00:05:34.420 --> 00:05:38.480
Iron Man nearly lost his life while trying
to defeat the Chitauri in The Avengers.

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:43.880
What would the future of the MCU have looked
like had Tony Stark's Iron Man died in the

00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:44.840
Battle of New York?

00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:49.250
Stark certainly left his mark on the Marvel
universe, and a lot of his contributions took

00:05:49.250 --> 00:05:50.460
place after The Avengers.

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:54.980
So many things would be different if the Iron
Avenger had kicked the bucket early.

00:05:55.300 --> 00:05:57.180
Would Ultron still have been invented?

00:05:57.580 --> 00:06:00.470
How would Peter Parker's Spider-Man have been
recruited to the team?

00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:01.240
Would he at all?

00:06:01.470 --> 00:06:06.240
Perhaps most importantly, who would've sacrificed
themselves to defeat Thanos at the end of

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:07.060
Avengers: Endgame?

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:10.560
The MCU without Tony Stark would be a bleak
place indeed.

00:06:11.240 --> 00:06:16.120
In Captain America: Civil War, Stark is tasked
with bringing in Captain America after an

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:18.960
incident involving a brainwashed Bucky Barnes.

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:23.940
Although Stark and his team manage to capture
Cap's compatriots, Rogers and Barnes end up

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:27.900
besting him in a final, friendship-severing
brawl in Siberia.

00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:32.060
Cap then goes on to free Hawkeye, Ant-Man,
Scarlet Witch and the Falcon.

00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:36.640
It's interesting to wonder what would've happened
had Stark won the Siberian showdown, arresting

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:40.880
Captain America and potentially revenge-killing
Winter Soldier for murdering his parents years

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:41.400
ago.

00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:46.300
Cap probably would've been sent to prison
with the rest of his team, and they would've

00:06:46.310 --> 00:06:49.639
conceivably been stuck there until the events
of Infinity War.

00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:51.760
Unless, of course, they managed to break out.

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:57.379
Hulk chose to fly away in a Quinjet after
the events of Age of Ultron, leaving his friends

00:06:57.380 --> 00:06:57.880
behind.

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:03.180
He somehow arrived on Sakaar, where he became
the Grandmaster's champion until he joined

00:07:03.180 --> 00:07:05.259
up with Thor in Thor: Ragnarok.

00:07:05.460 --> 00:07:09.620
Although Banner eventually returned to Earth,
a lot happened during his extended leave of

00:07:09.620 --> 00:07:10.120
absence.

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:14.960
Perhaps the most notable conflict was the
superhero Civil War, which pitted Captain

00:07:14.980 --> 00:07:16.480
America against Iron Man.

00:07:16.900 --> 00:07:20.120
What would've happened if Hulk had been around
when that went down?

00:07:20.380 --> 00:07:24.280
During Civil War, Stark mentioned that he
wished Banner was on Earth, assuming he would

00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:25.290
take his side.

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:27.540
"Be great if we had a Hulk right about now.

00:07:27.700 --> 00:07:28.320
Any shot?"

00:07:30.440 --> 00:07:31.920
"You really think he'd be on our side?"

00:07:33.140 --> 00:07:37.750
Despite Natasha's concerns, it's not hard
to imagine Hulk siding with Iron Man, which

00:07:37.750 --> 00:07:40.920
could have drastically tilted the scales toward
Team Stark.

00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:46.000
Seeing Hulk's inclusion in Civil War would
undoubtedly make for an action-packed episode

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:47.000
of What If...?

00:07:47.280 --> 00:07:52.360
If you think Erik Killmonger is the best villain
in the MCU to date, you aren't alone.

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:57.169
The Black Panther baddie was a force to be
reckoned with, even besting T'Challa in combat

00:07:57.169 --> 00:07:58.920
and claiming the Wakandan throne.

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:03.300
Fortunately for the rest of the world, T'Challa
lived and was able to defeat his long-lost

00:08:03.300 --> 00:08:03.880
cousin.

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:05.080
But what if he hadn't?

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:07.220
“Is this your king?

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:08.260
Huh?

00:08:10.320 --> 00:08:11.440
Is this your king?"

00:08:12.780 --> 00:08:17.719
Killmonger's main plan was to send advanced
Wakandan weaponry to groups that would incite

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:20.020
anarchy and overthrow governments around the
world.

00:08:20.440 --> 00:08:24.500
T'Challa and his allies just barely managed
to destroy the cargo ships before they could

00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:28.400
reach their targets, but it's interesting
to think about what would've happened if they

00:08:28.409 --> 00:08:28.900
had failed.

00:08:29.409 --> 00:08:33.900
For starters, this kind of widespread attack
on society would undoubtedly catch the attention

00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:34.480
of the Avengers.

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:39.600
Although the team would still be divided after
the events of Civil War, it's easy to imagine

00:08:39.610 --> 00:08:43.940
both squads putting their differences aside
to deal with Killmonger, especially considering

00:08:43.940 --> 00:08:47.700
T'Challa's solid relationships with both Captain
America and Iron Man.

00:08:48.280 --> 00:08:52.780
If the Avengers had attacked a Killmonger-led
Wakanda, they'd surely be in for a tough fight,

00:08:53.180 --> 00:08:56.800
which would make for one undeniably entertaining
episode of What If...?

00:08:57.480 --> 00:09:02.000
Earning the Soul Stone, arguably the most complex of the six Infinity Stones, is a bit

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:03.540
of a lose-lose scenario.

00:09:03.540 --> 00:09:06.860
In order to claim it, you have to sacrifice
the thing you love most.

00:09:06.860 --> 00:09:12.710
In Infinity War, Thanos killed Gamora, his
"favorite daughter," on Vormir as the means

00:09:12.710 --> 00:09:14.320
to add the gem to his gauntlet.

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:20.240
In Endgame's time heist, longtime pals Black
Widow and Hawkeye traveled to the gloomy planet

00:09:20.240 --> 00:09:23.580
in the past in order to claim a past version
of the stone.

00:09:23.900 --> 00:09:27.870
Although both tried to sacrifice their own
lives for the cause, it was ultimately Widow

00:09:27.870 --> 00:09:28.660
who made the jump.

00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:32.560
How would things have been different had Black
Widow lived and Hawkeye died instead?

00:09:32.860 --> 00:09:36.900
It would've been tough for her to have to
break the news to Clint's family after Hulk

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:41.940
snapped them back into existence, but her
presence means more to the future of the Avengers.

00:09:42.300 --> 00:09:46.540
After all, she seemed to be in charge of the
team after Thanos' snap, while Captain America

00:09:46.540 --> 00:09:50.480
led group therapy sessions and Tony Stark
started a family with Pepper.

00:09:50.960 --> 00:09:53.660
How would the future of the MCU change if
she had lived?

00:09:54.420 --> 00:09:59.280
Despite its slow decline in popularity over
the past few years, AMC's The Walking Dead

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:03.200
is still firmly marching on in the network's
schedule and the ratings.

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:07.480
How would you feel about another zombie show,
only this time, it takes place in the MCU?

00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:12.680
It turns out, Robert Kirkman, co-creator of
The Walking Dead comic book series, also wrote

00:10:12.680 --> 00:10:17.540
a five-issue miniseries about zombies invading
the Marvel universe in the early 2000s.

00:10:17.920 --> 00:10:20.900
Since then, the concept has been impossible
to put to rest.

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:26.300
Astute fans of the MCU have noticed that if
you look closely enough at the What If...?

00:10:26.300 --> 00:10:30.840
logo, you can make out a zombified Captain
America "hidden" behind the font.

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:35.450
This subtle clue led many to believe that
one episode of the animated series would play

00:10:35.450 --> 00:10:41.720
with the Marvel Zombies comics storyline,
which takes place on Earth-2149 in the Marvel

00:10:41.720 --> 00:10:42.720
multiverse.

00:10:42.730 --> 00:10:46.740
That theory turned out to be accurate, as
a preview has confirmed that zombies will

00:10:46.740 --> 00:10:48.320
be invading the MCU.

00:10:48.540 --> 00:10:49.780
The only question is how?

00:10:49.980 --> 00:10:54.520
Perhaps Thanos, whose primary goal centered
around population control, might choose a

00:10:54.530 --> 00:10:59.130
more creative way to eliminate half of the
universe's population by snapping zombies

00:10:59.130 --> 00:11:00.180
into existence.

00:11:00.360 --> 00:11:05.040
Or, given the obvious supernatural theme of
the undead, maybe a foe of Doctor Strange

00:11:05.040 --> 00:11:06.180
has something to do with it.

00:11:06.260 --> 00:11:10.500
Regardless, hopefully Thor remembers the one
important rule when it comes to dealing with

00:11:10.500 --> 00:11:11.040
zombies.

00:11:12.640 --> 00:11:15.200
"You should've gone for the head."

00:11:15.760 --> 00:11:17.700
